{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2229","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Slimes on a Line"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n$$$ slimes on a line, where slime $$$i$$$ is at position $$$a_i$$$ on the line. You will perform the following operation some number of times (possibly none):"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" select an integer $$$x$$$, then for each $$$j$$$ ($$$1 \\le j \\le n$$$): "},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"kind":"list"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$a_j \\lt x$$$ then do $$$a_j := a_j + 1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$a_j \\gt x$$$ then do $$$a_j := a_j - 1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$a_j = x$$$ then do nothing. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine the minimum number of operations to make all slimes occupy the same position."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 100$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each testcase contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\le n \\le 1000$$$) — the number of slimes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each testcase contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_{n}$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 1000$$$) — the initial positions of the slimes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$1000$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, output the minimum number of operations required to make all slimes occupy the same position."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n10\n5\n1 2 3 4 5\n5\n3 3 3 3 3\n6\n5 6 7 1 2 3\n2\n2 5\n4\n1 3 8 7\n4\n6 2 1 8\n3\n1 3 9\n5\n1 10 1 10 10\n8\n10 8 5 9 1 6 9 10\n2\n1 1000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n0\n3\n2\n4\n4\n4\n5\n5\n500\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Test Case 1:"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" We can perform $$$2$$$ operations, both with $$$x = 3$$$. The first operation updates the array of positions to $$$a = [2, 3, 3, 3, 4]$$$, and then the second operation updates it to $$$a = [3, 3, 3, 3, 3]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Test Case 2:"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" All the slimes are already at position $$$3$$$, and hence $$$0$$$ operations are needed."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"2229A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2229/problem/A"}